<title>BELGIUM: Belgian tax receipts up 4.0 pct in 11 mths to Nov.</title>
<headline>Belgian tax receipts up 4.0 pct in 11 mths to Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Belgian fiscal receipts were up 4.3 percent in November from November 1995 and up 4.0 percent in the first 11 months of 1996 from the same 1995 period, the Finance Ministry said in a statement on Monday.  </p>
<p>TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>				     Nov 96	 Nov 95     pct change</p>
<p>    Total			  147,647	141,588	4.3</p>
<p>    Direct taxation	     63,815	 73,015    -12.6</p>
<p>    VAT and similar taxes     45,778	 40,968     11.7</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>				     Jan-Nov 96   Jan-Nov 95 pct change</p>
<p>    Total			  2,015,077    1,937,125    4.0</p>
<p>    Direct taxation	    1,152.893    1,133,868    1.7</p>
<p>    VAT and similar taxes	530,925	510,533    4.0</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
